<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="PIC-24F:LE:24:default:default">
<!--
    GH-8777: "PIC24: signed branch lifts to a raw SBORROW flag idiom."
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8777

    The PIC24 spec models `bra ge` explicitly as the condition-flag identity
    N == V over the subtraction (V - K):
        cond = (SRL_N && SRL_OV) || (!SRL_N && !SRL_OV)        (== XNOR(N,V))
    where N = sign of (V - K)  (INT_SLESSEQUAL(0, V-K) / INT_SLESS(-1, V-K))
    and   V = INT_SBORROW(V, K)  (signed overflow).  XNOR(N,V) is the textbook
    signed `V >= K` test, but upstream has no rule for it, so the raw flag
    algebra survives into the rendered loop condition:

      for (iVar1 = 0; bVar2 = 0 <= iVar1 + -7,
          (bVar2 || !SBORROW2(iVar1,7)) && (!bVar2 || SBORROW2(iVar1,7));
          iVar1 = iVar1 + 1) { ... }

    Stage model: S3 "simplification-quiescence" (which algebraic/peephole rules
    fire).  kuna's RuleSborrowGe (group "analysis", gated by the default-off arch
    flag fold_flag_compare) recognizes the XNOR(N,V) tree in either De-Morgan
    dual form (AND-of-ORs or OR-of-ANDs) with N = sign(V-K) and V = SBORROW(V,K),
    and rewrites the whole boolean tree to INT_SLESSEQUAL(K, V) == `V s>= K`.
    Exposed by `option flagcompare on`.

    Pass 1 (default pipeline) reproduces the bug: the SBORROW2 flag idiom
    survives in the loop condition (assert #1).
    Pass 2 (after `option flagcompare on`) the loop condition is the clean
    signed comparison `7 <= iVar1` and no SBORROW2 remains (assert #2).

    Disassembly:
      0x000000 mov.w #0x0,W2
      0x000002 mov.w #0x7,W3
      0x000004 sub.w W2,W3,W12
      0x000006 bra   ge,0x10
      0x000008 mov.w #0x0,W0
      0x00000a mov.w W0,0x80
      0x00000c add.w W2,#0x1,W2
      0x00000e bra   0x4
      0x000010 return
-->
